WEBVTT

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.850
FUJISAWA FIRST (KANAGAWA)
VS. SHINTOKU (HYOGO)

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.770
Arashi! It's starting!

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.770
-<i>Aiming for a spot in the final four,</i>
-I'm coming!

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.150
-<i>Fujisawa First</i>
-Here's your tea.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.360
<i>takes the field for the top of the first.</i>

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.070
NO. 1 TAKAHIRO ARAMAKI (2ND YEAR)

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.870
<i>Here's the ace pitcher who's the focus
of the tournament, Takahiro Aramaki!</i>

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.370
<i>It looks like some scouts
from the major leagues</i>

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.620
<i>are here to watch him today.</i>

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.330
Where am I?

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.500
Mom? Where are you?

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.500
Mom?

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.010
If you're awake, hurry up and follow me.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.340
We're about to sink.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:39.680
There's no more time!

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:46.980
This way!

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:04.370
Why...

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:08.710
<i>When you all wake up,
you may be in heaven...</i>

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.720
<i>or you may be in hell.</i>

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:23.810
<i>No matter the case,
I hope you will all strive to stay alive.</i>

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.810
Hurry, this way! Get onboard!

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:29.810
Hurry up!

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:07.910
SPRING BEGINS

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:15.790
Are you all right?

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.710
Get on the boat!

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.210
Are you okay? Grab on!

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.760
Oh, look at Mr. Cool Guy!

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.350
Do you always brave danger
to help complete strangers?

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.680
It's human nature to want to help others.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.680
I wouldn't do it.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:35.440
Fine. If you get into trouble,
I'll just leave you behind.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.690
Some hero you are.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:38.820
Get up here!

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.900
We have to move away
before that sinking ship takes us with it!

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.780
That's my bag...

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:50.950
Why is it here?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.040
Are there any others?

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.920
No, it's just the four of us.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.510
I didn't see anyone else.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.020
If you're going to puke, do it outside.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.190
Don't worry. I've got an empty stomach!

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.560
It's weird.
I ate a lot of barbecue last night.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.070
Last night...

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:27.030
All of my favorite dishes,
and so much of them.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.290
Seems like things have calmed down.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.500
Can anyone explain what happened?

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:48.010
I don't even remember leaving my house,
much less getting on any ship.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.930
I was asleep in my bed.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.930
How did I end up here?

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:54.520
Someone tell me! What happened?

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:00.020
I'm in the same situation.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:03.480
Same here. I woke up on that ship.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.400
You're pretty quick on your feet
for someone who just woke up.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.910
Really? So, what's your story?

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:14.540
All I remember is eating a ton of barbecue
before I went to bed. That's it.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.040
So, we've all got amnesia?

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.750
Where are our families?

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.630
Right now, we need to find a place
and make landfall.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.140
Look! There's an island right over there!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.770
It looks like a cat.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.940
Now that you mention it, it sure does.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:43.020
I hope Mom is looking after my cat.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.900
If we don't do something,
we'll crash into that cliff!

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.950
Use these. We need to start rowing!

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.110
What?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.910
Listen,
we need to get out of this current!

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.700
Damn it! Why did I get stuck in this mess?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.160
Shut up and row!

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:58.710
What is it?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.460
I thought I saw something in the water.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.540
We'll catch it and eat it later.
Just focus on rowing for now.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:04.590
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:08.260
Boys, unless you match our pace,
we'll just end up going in circles.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.220
We know that!

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.970
Looks like this is a dead-end.

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.980
I'll go see if we can
get to the top from here. Stay put.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.860
Nice ass, lady.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.740
Save that for later.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.870
Dang, she's so mature.
She brushed me off like it was nothing.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:44.130
What a flat ass.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.840
Little girls are so lame.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.550
I was hoping for a shriek or a "No!"

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.550
Cut it out.
You're making a bad impression.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:54.550
Whatever, I don't give a damn.
I know I'm a total asshole.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.600
You climb ahead of us.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:57.930
Okay, fine.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.430
Sorry.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.440
The sun is coming up.
East must be that way.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.700
I wonder if there's anyone else
on this island?

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:13.990
What do you think?

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:14.990
What?

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:18.450
Oh, I don't know.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.200
Sorry.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:24.080
Why are you always apologizing?
You don't have to be so polite.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.040
Oh, I know. Let's all introduce ourselves.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.670
My name is Arashi Aota.
I'm a sophomore in high school.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.680
I'm Natsu Iwashimizu.
I'm a high school freshman.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.430
Nice to meet you.
I'm Semimaru Asai. I'm 18.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:39.560
With a name like that,
your parents must be poets.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:43.440
What? What are you talking about?
I was born in summer, that's all.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.020
Don't you dare call me "Cicada Boy"
or anything like that!

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:49.190
Besides, "summer" and "cicada" make
a good pair, right?

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:50.530
Let's be friends!

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.240
You get bullied a lot, don't you?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.450
I'm a bully myself.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.780
You're my new prey.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:01.620
That's enough, Cicada Boy.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.620
What? Now, you've done it.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:05.750
Bastard!

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.290
You prick.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.340
Am I interrupting your playtime?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.050
My name is Botan Saotome.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.760
Since I'm the oldest, I'm in charge.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.430
Let's start by looking for water.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.890
We'll split into two groups.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.720
You're coming with me.

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:28.690
Make sure you don't get lost.
We'll meet back here later.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.990
You're pretty tough, Ms. Iwashimizu!

00:09:34.070 --> 00:09:35.150
What?

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:39.320
I know some people who would be
a big, sobbing mess in this situation.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:41.490
<i>Is he talking about his girlfriend?</i>

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.330
I'm not really that tough.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:45.250
<i>Crying would shift the attention to me.</i>

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:48.000
<i>I'm not assertive enough to do that.</i>

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:51.340
<i>I've always been uncomfortable
in situations like that.</i>

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.880
There's a waterfall! Great!

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.090
Can you tell the other two?

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.890
If you call them from back there,
they'll hear you.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:01.220
Okay.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.520
I can't yell very loudly.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.730
Hey, Big Sis Botan,

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.230
I get the feeling you know something
about all this.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:11.900
Well, that's hard to say.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:16.400
From my perspective,
you seem oddly calm about everything.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:20.910
You're a tough one.
I love that kind of thing.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:25.290
Let's have some fun.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.830
Do you have a death wish?

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.170
I guess you do.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.130
I'm just kidding.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:35.630
That knife will come in handy
from here on out.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.630
Take good care of it.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.140
Dang, she's pretty frightening.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:45.390
Oh, there they are.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.140
I wonder if they'll hear me.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:52.730
What's wrong?

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.110
Well...

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:59.200
<i>He was so nice to me earlier,
I hope this doesn't make him hate me.</i>

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.530
Let me handle this.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:04.370
Water! We found water!

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:07.540
Really? We'll be right there!

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.210
If a helicopter flies by,
they'll see this.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:18.760
Let's hope so.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.300
More importantly, where's the food?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.800
I'm starving over here!

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.680
You're right. Let's split up
and try to find something edible.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.270
Okay, I'll search over here.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.060
Semimaru, gather some wood
and start a fire.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:36.270
Why is she ordering me around?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:38.740
Hey, twerp!

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:42.780
Strip those down into thin pieces for me.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:43.780
What?

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.620
Do what I say,
or I'll give you hell, dummy!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.290
Okay.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.830
<i>I have to do something
to prove myself useful.</i>

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:57.130
<i>Otherwise, I'll just be a burden.</i>

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.800
What are you doing?

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:02.470
I thought it was clear
we were going to search for food.

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:05.350
Well, I was told to do this.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.720
By who? Semimaru?

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:08.850
Yes.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.640
What is all this?
What will you do with it?

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:15.230
I don't know.

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:18.070
You don't know? Are you an idiot?

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:20.570
Don't you know how to think for yourself?

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.990
Don't you understand our situation?

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.530
We have to think for ourselves
in order to survive!

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.450
I'm sorry.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.290
Look at people when you talk to them.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.790
Otherwise, you'll only invite trouble.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:34.870
I'm sorry.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.750
All you ever do is apologize.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:41.050
Hurry up and go!

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.840
Find your own food, at the very least!

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.640
Those are bananas, I think.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:01.400
That's shocking. I'm totally useless.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.900
That's what I get
for never climbing trees.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:05.910
Okay, how about this?

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.740
<i>I have to do what I'm told.</i>

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:13.160
<i>Otherwise, they'll just abandon me.</i>

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.040
<i>I'll be left behind.</i>

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.890
Move, legs! I have to get away!

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.570
Arashi! Save me, Arashi!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.610
I found it.

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:50.620
I outran them.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.760
It's... a monster!

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:17.480
Hana! Are you okay?

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.980
Tsunomata, behind you!

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.620
Thanks for the save, Hana.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.540
Right back at you. Thanks.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:41.040
Mr. Yanagi, what are you doing?

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:44.920
I'm going to burn them.
It's the most efficient method.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.420
We can't do that.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.930
All we need to do is
get some food and water.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.600
There's no reason to exterminate
the insects.

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:54.560
An environmentalist, are we?

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:59.520
Listen, girlie. We're not in a position
to worry about those kinds of issues.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:00.940
Don't!

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:03.360
Do you want to die out here?

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:06.320
If you ask me, I'm with Hana on this.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:08.400
Needless killing is unacceptable.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:11.860
If you destroy the plants,
we'll have even more problems.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.870
I expected more of you, Tsunomata.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:16.990
Let's get out of here.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.500
I don't take orders from you!

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:21.120
Mr. Yanagi!

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:23.630
Shit!

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:25.960
Damn bugs!

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:27.880
Are you okay?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.220
Goddamn it! This is your fault!

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.550
Welcome back, Hana.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.720
Thanks for going out there.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:35.930
We made it back.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:39.350
Haru, Fujiko, here.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:40.850
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.230
And for you, Momotaro.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:43.350
Thanks!

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.650
Is everyone all right?

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.230
Stupid brat. Do we look all right?

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:49.940
That's the last time
I'm going there to get water.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.570
The bugs were all over the place.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:57.240
It's been two weeks since we came here.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:00.410
We haven't seen a plane or a ship
the whole damn time.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:04.080
That means help isn't coming
no matter how long we wait for it.

00:16:04.170 --> 00:16:07.420
We're getting out of here right now.
Get ready to move!

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:10.630
-Right now?
-I can't stand another minute here!

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:13.380
I think we should stay put
for the rest of today.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.390
What? Why?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.140
It smells like rain.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.020
The weather is just fine!

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.940
For now, but I don't think it will last.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:27.860
We should trust our instincts
while we're in--

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:29.820
Hana!

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:34.490
Have you forgotten?
I'm the leader of this group.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:36.820
My orders must be obeyed.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:39.330
I'm telling you because it's dangerous.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.580
What?

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.290
Hold on a minute.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:46.500
If you're the leader here,
then I demand you take us back home!

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:47.880
Then we--

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.500
Shut up.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:53.050
I've had enough of
your snarky remarks, too.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.550
Calm down. Let's not get violent, pal.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.970
Tsunomata, who are you calling "pal"?

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.180
No violence, please, sir.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:01.720
Get it through your heads.
I'm in charge here!

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:03.730
Stop wasting time and get to work!

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:06.650
Once everything is ready,
we're leaving immediately!

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:14.860
Do you think there's land somewhere?

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.450
I don't know, but I sure hope so.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:22.290
We don't know where we're headed,
and we have no destination.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.250
Hey! You girls over there!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.710
Quit talking and start rowing!

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:46.100
Hey, Chisa. How is Hibari doing?

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.770
Oh, hi, Hana.

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.770
She's still the same.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.360
Her body is freezing cold,
it's almost like she's dead.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:56.610
Sometimes I get worried and grab her hand,

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.200
but she still has a pulse.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.410
I see.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.250
Hey. What the heck are you doing?

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.500
I'm keeping watch.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.180
What's wrong? You're no match for me!

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:19.180
<i>He reeks.</i>

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:23.720
Thanks to you, I'm in a lot of pain
from the bug that stung me!

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:24.720
Get off of me!

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:26.850
-<i>Not just the smell.</i>
-You always talk like a big shot,

00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.940
-<i>Something is wrong with him!</i>
-but just look at you.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:30.940
You don't have the strength to match me!

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:32.690
Cut it out!

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.690
I'll make sure you never disobey me again!

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.370
Damn! The raft is going to split apart!

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:44.910
Everybody, grab on to something!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:46.620
What's wrong?

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:48.750
Hibari got swept away by the waves!

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:52.710
-Leave her be!
-You can't be serious!

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.750
She was as good as dead anyway.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:56.800
Instead, grab some rope
and tie down our supplies!

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.170
I'm not letting her die.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.090
What?

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:00.090
Hana?

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:02.090
It's okay, I'll catch up!

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.680
Great. Less dead weight
I need to worry about.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:09.140
What are you staring at?
Get over here and help me!

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.610
<i>Hibari.</i>

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.570
<i>Hibari!</i>

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:29.290
That's...

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:34.040
We're right back where we started.
The damn island of bugs!

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:36.090
We were washed all the way back here?

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:39.130
I think they've noticed us.

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.930
Hey, Hana. Give me that girl.

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:44.220
-What?
-She'll never wake up.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:45.680
So, what are you going to do?

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:47.100
Use her as bait.

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.930
It should buy us
plenty of time to get out of here.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:52.020
Are you insane?

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.480
We don't have time for this.
Hand her over!

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:59.320
Just do as I say!
I'm doing this to keep us all alive!

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:00.360
No way!

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:03.030
I'm sick of you damn idiots.
Enough! Give her to me!

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.910
Mr. Yanagi, are you crazy?

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:05.950
Stop it!

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.200
-I won't let you hurt her!
-Quit whining!

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:09.250
I told you to stop!

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:11.870
You bitch!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:16.460
We have to save him.

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.210
Take care of Hibari.

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:19.170
What?

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:21.260
You can't!

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.880
Let's get out of here.
There's nothing we can do.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.680
-But...
-Forget him.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.680
Let's go back to the beach.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:42.740
We're right back where we started again.

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:45.490
The current must have
dragged us back here.

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:46.870
It's like we're trapped.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.580
This sucks.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:54.830
I abandoned him.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.590
No, you didn't! It's not your fault, Hana.

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.040
He got what he deserved.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.800
If we didn't do anything,
he would have killed Hibari.

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.310
It's not all bad news.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:18.940
A fair amount
of our food supply is still safe.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.860
Would anyone like to eat?

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.410
Mr. Yanagi...

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.640
Good, you're all awake.

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:57.650
Unami?

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:00.190
Everybody line up. No lollygagging.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:02.900
But... why are you here?

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:06.990
Since you're a bunch of wusses,
they decided to add an adult to the group.

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:17.040
Ango! This isn't like you guys!

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.460
Hey, don't--

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:30.970
You bastards!
